      "writtenOn": "2022-04-27T21:14:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not wild about this idiom. If you only have one extension, just writing the declaration out should be simple and quick. It could probably even be a one-liner. If you have more than one extension, using this macro will be awkward at best. I think just typing out the definition would make it more obvious what\u0027s going on in the code.\n\nIf you want to make the emulator setup shorter, I\u0027d prefer a function defined to return a `struct tcpci_src_emul_data`. If I\u0027m not mistaken, that would also avoid the need to declare `tcpci_src_emul_ops` in this header file, which would be nice.",
